.TH FORK 2 "August 1, 1992"
.ds ]W POSIX 1003.1
.SH NAME
fork, vfork \- create a new process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ft B
#include <sys/types.h>
.sp
pid_t fork(void);
.ft R
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fIfork\fP function causes creation of a new process (\fIvfork\fR is another name for \fIfork\fR).  
The new process (child
process) is an exact copy of the calling process except for the following:
.in +5n
.sp
The child process has a unique process ID.
.sp
The child process has a different parent process ID (i.e.,
the process ID of the parent process).
.sp
The child process has its own copy of the parent's descriptors.
These descriptors reference the same underlying objects, so that,
for instance, file pointers in file objects are shared between
the child and the parent, so that an \fIlseek\fP(2)
on a descriptor in the child process can affect a subsequent
\fIread\fP(2) or \fIwrite\fP(2) by the parent.
This descriptor copying is also used by the shell to
establish standard input and output for newly created processes
as well as to set up pipes.
.sp
The child processes resource utilizations are set to 0;
see
.IR setrlimit (2).
.PP
.in -5n
For POSIX applications the following differences between the child
and parent process also apply:
.in +5n
.sp
File locks previously set by the parent are not inherited by the child.
.sp
Pending alarms are cleared for the child process.
.sp
The set of pending signals for the child process is initialized to the empty
set.
.SH "RETURN VALUE
Upon successful completion, \fIfork\fP returns a value
of 0 to the child process and returns the process ID of the child
process to the parent process.  Otherwise, a value of \-1 is returned
to the parent process, no child process is created, and the global
variable \fIerrno\fP is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
The \fIfork\fP function will fail and no child process will be created if
one or more of the following are true:
.TP 15
[EAGAIN]
The system-imposed limit on the total
number of processes under execution would be exceeded.
.TP 15
[EAGAIN]
The system-imposed limit MAXUPRC (\fI<sys/param.h>) \fPon the total number of
processes under execution by a single user would be exceeded.
.TP 15
[ENOMEM]
There is insufficient swap space for the new process.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
execve(2), wait(2)
